{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the harsh sunlight feeling…different. Sharper. He sat up in bed, the floral patterned comforter looking unnervingly pixelated. His bedroom, usually cluttered with books and half-finished projects, was rendered with an almost cartoonish clarity. A notification box, complete with a cheerful chime, popped into his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1 Achieved!\" Panic clawed at his throat. He tried to grab his glasses, but his hand passed right through them. He looked down at his body - no longer the slightly paunchy form he knew, but lean, muscular, and clad in what appeared to be generic adventurer’s garb. A shimmering quest marker floated above his head, pointing towards the forest outside. This wasn't a dream. This was…a video game. A ridiculously detailed, unsettlingly real video game.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously stepped outside, the grass feeling strangely springy beneath his boots. A small, wooden signpost stood nearby, displaying a crudely drawn map of the surrounding area. The trees were impossibly green, the birds sang with a synthesized quality, and the air hummed with an underlying digital buzz. A small, furry creature with oversized ears scampered past, leaving a faint trail of glittering particles. Arthur felt a surge of both terror and a bizarre, reluctant excitement. He had no idea how he got here, or how to get back, but one thing was clear: he was now a character in someone else's story, and he had a quest to complete. He squinted at the quest marker, a faint whisper in his mind urging him forward. \"Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin Caves.\" Great. Just great.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.4037037789821625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00023040501400828362}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08387291431427002}, {"token": "▁harsh", "logprob": -1.0